menu "WIFI 8711 (AT-over-SPI) module config"
	config WIFI_8711
		bool "WiFi 8711 AT-over-SPI support"
		default n
	help
		This option enables the WiFi 8711 AT-over-SPI module: the SPI master
		driver toward the 8711 WiFi AT slave chip, the AT-over-SPI command
		engine and the SPI/TCP throughput test. Enabled by the wifi_8711 snippet
		(applications/watch/snippets/wifi_8711), which also supplies the
		wifi_8711_device / wifi_8711_resources devicetree nodes the SPI
		master binds to.

	config WIFI_8711_ROLE_MASTER
		bool "WiFi 8711 SPI master role"
		depends on WIFI_8711
		default y
	help
		Build the SPI master side (drives the 8711 slave over SPI DMA). This is
		the only role the watch supports; keep it enabled.

	config WIFI_8711_ROLE_SLAVE
		bool "WiFi 8711 SPI slave role"
		depends on WIFI_8711
		default n
	help
		Build the SPI slave side. No slave implementation exists on the watch,
		so this stays disabled.

	config WIFI_8711_TEST
		bool "WiFi 8711 shell test commands"
		depends on WIFI_8711 && SHELL
		default n
	help
		Register the `wifi8711` shell command group (SPI role init, AT WLCONN /
		WLDISCONN, and the SPI+TCP throughput test) so the flows previously
		triggered by host commands in app_cmd.c can be driven from a UART
		console. Replaces the CMD_SPI_INIT / CMD_AT_CMD_WLCONN /
		CMD_SPI_TCP_TP_TEST handling.

endmenu
